<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-consignment-photographs-2008> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P138i_has_representation> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-consignment-photographs-2008#visual-item> .
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-consignment-photographs-2008> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Sun & Rain Works holds eleven digital photographs, taken in a single session on 2008-08-08, that document a matted black-and-white photographic print in the studio's possession. The sequence records the print recto, the mount, the verso with its backing and hanging wire, and a close-up of the verso credit block. In one frame the print is photographed together with a copy of Andy Warhol's 'The Philosophy of Andy Warhol (From A to B and Back Again)', placed upright and facing the camera. The close-up of the verso shows a printed credit block reading 'Photograph by Ansel Adams for The American Trust Company', a negative number beginning '1-SF-', the beginning of a handwritten title 'San Francisco fr...', and a hand-inked annotation 'Wells Fargo Bank' written over the struck-through word 'THE'. These markings correspond, in four independent particulars, to the markings recorded in the public Sotheby's catalogue entry for lot 16 of Photographs, sale N08533 (2009) - the Ansel Adams print 'San Francisco from Twin Peaks'. The photographs therefore evidence that a print bearing the markings described in the lot-16 catalogue entry was in the studio's possession approximately seven months before that sale, and that it was documented there alongside an art-referential object. They do not establish the identity of the consignor of record, and they establish no precedence over any later artist, work, or event." .
